=== (A) sum rules on random N-band finite-range networks (W = B(k)^dag B(k) + m^2, range 2) ===
N= 2: <sum_n u_n''>_BZ = +2.2e-16;  sum_n [f_n(pi) - f_n(-pi)] (Hellmann-Feynman) = +2.2e-10;  max_n |<u_n''>_BZ| = 1.5e-15  (scale max u'' = 13)
N= 3: <sum_n u_n''>_BZ = -8.1e-14;  sum_n [f_n(pi) - f_n(-pi)] (Hellmann-Feynman) = +1.3e-09;  max_n |<u_n''>_BZ| = 9.3e-14  (scale max u'' = 67)
N= 5: <sum_n u_n''>_BZ = -5.9e-14;  sum_n [f_n(pi) - f_n(-pi)] (Hellmann-Feynman) = +4.4e-10;  max_n |<u_n''>_BZ| = 1.9e-13  (scale max u'' = 174)
N= 8: <sum_n u_n''>_BZ = +7.7e-13;  sum_n [f_n(pi) - f_n(-pi)] (Hellmann-Feynman) = -1.8e-09;  max_n |<u_n''>_BZ| = 7.4e-13  (scale max u'' = 351)
N=16: <sum_n u_n''>_BZ = -4.5e-13;  sum_n [f_n(pi) - f_n(-pi)] (Hellmann-Feynman) = -8.9e-09;  max_n |<u_n''>_BZ| = 7.5e-13  (scale max u'' = 1225)
-> the band-summed zone average of the Hessian is 0 for every finite N (telescoping / periodic tr W):
   the zone-averaged boost anomaly sum_n <u_n'' - beta> = -beta N, i.e. -beta per mode, whatever the network.
   (For band-sorted labels each band's distributional average is already 0; a tower-like band with u'' = beta
    inside must pay with kink deltas at touchings, as SLAC pays with its face delta.)

=== (B) C1's face-touching two-band network is a folded fine chain of spacing a/2 ===
max |{eps(k), eps(k+2pi)} - {E_-(k), E_+(k)}| = 1.8e-15
smoothness of eps(K) on the 4pi-periodic extended zone: |Fourier coeff| at 200, 400, 800: 2.4e-10 1.4e-13 4.5e-18  (super-algebraic decay: one smooth fine band)
closure residual |f - K|: lowest band (|K|<=pi) max 5.23e-12; partner at the fine face K -> +-2pi: |f - K| = 6.2825 (= pi N with N = 2: 6.2832)
zone-averaged boost anomaly over both bands <u''-1> = -1.0000; on the partner band (|K|>pi) <u''-1> = -2.000; lowest band <u''-1> = +1.05e-12
-> the C1 two-band construction IS a fine lattice of spacing a/2 (one smooth fine band, folded); its face
   touching is the folding, and the 'partner-band' problem is the fine lattice's own face floor (pi N, A ~ -N).

